{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs GNU C++ code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following GNU C++ code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nProf. Vasechkin wants to represent positive integer n as a sum of addends, where each addends is an integer number containing only 1s. For example, he can represent 121 as 121=111+11+\u20131. Help him to find the least number of digits 1 in such sum.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the GNU C++ code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\nlong long INF = 1e18;\nlong long ans = 0;\nvector<long long> dpr;\nlong long solve(long long n){\n\tif (n==0) return 0;\n\tif (n<dpr.size() && dpr[n]) return dpr[n];\n\tlong long lastdif = INF;\n\tlong long x = 1, i=0;\n\twhile (abs(x-n)<=lastdif){\n\t\tlastdif = abs(x-n);\n\t\tx=x*10+1;\n\t\ti++;\n\t}\n\tx/=10;\n\tif (x>n && x/10) {\n\t\tif (n<dpr.size())return dpr[n]=min(i+solve(abs(x-n)),i-1+solve(abs(x/10-n)));\n\t\treturn min(i+solve(abs(x-n)),i-1+solve(abs(x/10-n)));\n\t}\n\tif (n<dpr.size())\n\treturn dpr[n]= i+solve(abs(x-n));\n\treturn i+solve(abs(x-n));\n}\nint main(){\n#ifdef NEKROLM\n\tfreopen(\"input.txt\",\"r\",stdin);\n\tfreopen(\"output.txt\",\"w\",stdout);\n#endif\n\tios_base::sync_with_stdio(false);\n\tlong long n; cin >> n;\n\tdpr.resize(1e8);\n\tcout << solve(n);\n\n\treturn 0;\n}\n\n\n\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nlong long solve(long long n) {\n    if (n == 0) return 0;\n    \n    vector<long long> dp(n + 1, 0);\n    dp[0] = 0;\n    \n    for (long long i = 1; i <= n; i++) {\n        long long x = 1;\n        long long count = 1;\n        dp[i] = i; // worst case: use 1+1+...+1 (i times)\n        \n        while (x <= i) {\n            long long diff = i - x;\n            dp[i] = min(dp[i], count + dp[diff]);\n            x = x * 10 + 1;\n            count++;\n        }\n        \n        // Also consider using a number with one more digit (like 111...1) and subtracting\n        x = x / 10; // go back to previous x\n        count--;\n        if (x > 0) {\n            long long next_x = x * 10 + 1;\n            if (next_x <= 2 * i) { // only consider if it's not too far\n                dp[i] = min(dp[i], count + 1 + dp[next_x - i]);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    return dp[n];\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios_base::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    cout << solve(n);\n    return 0;\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.7\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-9.536738616588991e-07, -0.00019059749320149422, -2.0265558760002023e-06, 0.0, -3.2186455882765586e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -6.592056161025539e-05, -7.986990567587782e-06, -9.059865078597795e-06, -2.145764938177308e-06, -2.3841830625315197e-06, -0.5759483575820923, -3.4570634852570947e-06, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -0.11282341182231903, -0.17168360948562622, -8.785339014139026e-05, -0.2958221137523651, -0.00029202012228779495, -5.722029527532868e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.026317283511161804, 0.0,